500	+/* Builds the unmodified goop.c with HAVE_JWXYZ defined after the framework
501	+ * headers, which selects the code that draws each layer as filled polygons in
502	+ * order. The other path needs X colour planes and GXclear with a plane mask,
503	+ * which the canvas (RGB565, no spare bits) cannot give.
504	+ *
505	+ * Single precision (the S3's FPU is single-precision only, so `double` maths
506	+ * runs in software) with decimal literals made floats at build time, and the
507	+ * blobs' polygons filled in float (hacks/float_polygon.h): the shim's fill
508	+ * divides in double for every edge on every row.
509	+ *
510	+ * Upstream draws each frame into a window-sized pixmap and copies it to the
511	+ * window. The canvas is only pushed once the step is done, so nothing can tear:
512	+ * the pixmap is the window itself, and the copy is skipped (a full-frame
513	+ * PSRAM copy and 434 KB less memory). A one-bit pixmap (its xor mode) stays a
514	+ * real one. */
515	+#include <math.h>
516	+#include <stdio.h>
